WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.362
Where are agencies?

2
00:00:01.362 --> 00:00:05.705
This path assumes a civilian
agency at FedRAMP Moderate,

3
00:00:05.705 --> 00:00:10.601
most often with a Microsoft 365
GCC tenant and commercial Azure.

4
00:00:10.601 --> 00:00:15.996
Its scripts are often older than the
current tools: AzureAD or MSOnline cmdlets,

5
00:00:15.996 --> 00:00:20.575
a client secret in a scheduled task,
a host name written into the code.

6
00:00:20.575 --> 00:00:24.333
For what this module relies on,
GCC is the same as commercial:

7
00:00:24.333 --> 00:00:26.710
the worldwide sign-in and Graph hosts,

8
00:00:26.710 --> 00:00:31.618
app registration in the worldwide Entra
admin center, and the standard token

9
00:00:31.618 --> 00:00:36.450
exchange audience when a managed identity
is an app's federated credential.

10
00:00:36.450 --> 00:00:39.497
For each Graph API,
check the global service

11
00:00:39.497 --> 00:00:42.375
column of the page's national cloud table.

12
00:00:42.375 --> 00:00:47.461
GCC needs no endpoint change, but it can
lack features commercial tenants have,

13
00:00:47.461 --> 00:00:50.825
and Cloud Boundary and
Landing Zone keeps that list.

14
00:00:50.825 --> 00:00:55.537
The interim paths: rewrite retired-module
scripts on Graph PowerShell,

15
00:00:55.537 --> 00:00:59.520
and use a certificate on premises
until the server is on Arc.
